> And a gift is anything your god gives you? e.g. spellbook, weapon...

A gift is anything your god gave you from #offer.  Books *never*
come that way, only artifact weapons.

When #praying you can get a "pat on the head" benefit.  The possible
benefits are intrinsics including AC points, books and so on.  Exactly
once per game a #pray can result in an artifact - crowning.  I would
have to check int he code to see if that one increments the gift
counter.
But books never do increment the gift counter.

The interesting trick in counting gifts and artifacts separately is the
number of non-gift artifacts has no effect on the *first* gift.  The
two
numbers are multiplied together and then added.  Multiply by zero
and the result is zero.  So finding an artifact on the floor (probably
in a shop) or getting the one if the Quest or naming a couple or
getting certain artifacts from specific very mean monsters, none of
those have any effect at all on your first gift.  But they all have an
effect on the second and subsequent gift.

So if your goal is to collect as many artifacts as possible, avoid
getting any at all until you have gotten as many gifts as you think
you ever will, then switch to getting them by other means.  But if
all you've ever want is that one from the first gift (a wizard may only
want Magicbane) then get other ones any way you like.



